"Passing the oath ceremony at Welcome End is the final step in becoming declared."
"Oaths are shaped by shared memories witnessed in preparation; the leader's questions recall them."
"One memory, a wizard's vengeful torture, defines the oath against purposeless harm."
"Emotional release is not an acceptable purpose for harm under the oaths."
"Newcomers wear white warming robes; each sits on a spot of light, declared near the edge."
"The leader asks 'Tell us who you are and what you bring to us. Why have you come to this place?'"
"The welcome: 'none were born among us and all of us were strangers once. Sit with us now.'"
"One deemed wrong-hearted is rejected from the communion and may try again after reflection."
"The ceremony closes with a jug of the waters of many lands, including the first Rapport's."
"Knights periodically renew their oaths at such ceremonies."
